  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 9,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.089,
            0.454,
            0.104
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 11.4"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.105,
            0.9,
            0.172
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The potential difference between the terminals of an electric heater is 60 V when it draws a current of 4 A from the source. What current will the heater draw if the potential difference is increased to 120 V? Solution",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.172,
            0.828,
            0.189
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We are given, potential difference "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "V = 6 0   \\mathrm { V } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " current "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "I   =   4   \\mathrm { A }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.196,
            0.726,
            0.229
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "According to Ohm’s law,",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "R=\\frac{V}{I}=\\frac{60\\  V }{4\\  A }=15\\ \\Omega"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.233,
            0.899,
            0.267
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When the potential difference is increased to 120 V the current is given by",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.272,
            0.556,
            0.307
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "{ \\mathrm { c u r r e n t } } = { \\frac { V } { R } } = { \\frac { 1 2 0 { \\mathrm { ~ V ~ } } } { 1 5 \\; \\Omega } } = 8 { \\mathrm { ~ A ~ } } ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.313,
            0.708,
            0.331
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The current through the heater becomes 8 A.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.344,
            0.454,
            0.36
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 11.5"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.359,
            0.9,
            0.426
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Resistance of a metal wire of length 1 m is 26",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Ω "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "at",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathbb { C }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". If the diameter of the wire is 0.3 mm, what will be the resistivity of the metal at that temperature? Using Table 11.2, predict the material of the wire.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.429,
            0.401,
            0.444
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solution"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.445,
            0.899,
            0.478
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We are given the resistance R of the",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{wire}=26\\ \\Omega"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", the diameter",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "d = 0.3\\  mm  = 3 \\times 10^{-4}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "m, and the length l of the wire = 1 m.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.478,
            0.899,
            0.516
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore, from Eq. (11.10), the resistivity of the given metallic wire is",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\rho \\quad = \\quad ( R A / l ) \\quad \\equiv \\quad ( R \\pi d ^ { 2 } / 4 l )"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.519,
            0.618,
            0.537
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Substitution of values in this gives",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.539,
            0.504,
            0.556
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "\\rho = 1.84 \\times 10^{-6}   \\Omega    m"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.559,
            0.898,
            0.595
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The resistivity of the metal at",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathbf { C }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "is",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 . 8 4 \\: \\times \\: 1 0 ^ { - 6 } \\Omega"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "m",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". From "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Table 11.2, we see that this is the resistivity of manganese.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.608,
            0.454,
            0.623
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 11.6"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.623,
            0.9,
            0.691
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A wire of given material having length l and area of cross-section A has a resistance of 4",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Ω. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What would be the resistance of another wire of the same material having length l/2 and area of cross-section 2A? Solution",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.693,
            0.427,
            0.709
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For first wire",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.312,
            0.715,
            0.474,
            0.747
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_18.jpg",
          "content": "R_{1} = \\rho \\frac{l}{A} = 4\\Omega"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.311,
            0.749,
            0.495,
            0.767
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now for second wire",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.312,
            0.772,
            0.546,
            0.808
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_20.jpg",
          "content": "R_{2} = \\rho \\frac{l/2}{2A} = \\frac{1}{4} \\rho \\frac{l}{A}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.312,
            0.814,
            0.449,
            0.845
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_21.jpg",
          "content": "R _ { _ 2 } = \\frac { 1 } { 4 } \\quad R _ { _ L }"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.312,
            0.848,
            0.384,
            0.867
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_22.jpg",
          "content": "R _ { 2 } { = } 1 \\Omega"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.311,
            0.869,
            0.634,
            0.886
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The resistance of the new wire is 1",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ω."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.831,
            0.916,
            0.9,
